{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":63391,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"a49ba823-1886-52d6-aaf2-ec391fec4481","total_cost_usd":0.531041,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10754,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6216,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10754,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6216,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10754},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5041,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005141000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6216,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10754,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5259,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-h2-reviewer-fable-38\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:4da6848cdd3a5d975d87\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The input file contains exactly 24 data rows with 24 unique stream_code values (PG01 through PG24), so each independent unit occupies exactly one row and no unit is repeated in the file.\",\"observed_value\":{\"n_rows\":24,\"n_unique_stream_codes\":24,\"duplicates\":0},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"stream_code,catchment_area_km2,glacier_cover_pct,mean_elev_m,doc_june_mg_per_l,doc_sept_mg_per_l\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"PG01,4.82,31.5,2418,2.14,2.63\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"PG24,18.36,13.8,2071,4.24,3.86\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description designates stream_code as the independent-unit column, defines one trial as one row, and states the paired visits are stored side by side in a single record, so the wide layout keeps repeated measurements out of separate rows.\",\"observed_value\":\"independent unit = stream_code; one trial = one row; both visits in one record\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":7,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one proglacial stream, carrying its catchment descriptors together with its single June and its single September dissolved organic carbon measurement\\nIndependent unit column: stream_code\\nOne trial is: one row\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"Both visit values sit side by side in the same record, so a stream never occupies more than one line of the file.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly guards against duplicated independent units by raising an error if any stream_code repeats, then reduces each stream's two visits to one signed change so exactly one observation per unit enters the test.\",\"observed_value\":\"duplicate guard present; one delta per stream computed\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":34,\"end_line\":36,\"quoted_text\":\"codes = [row[\\\"stream_code\\\"] for row in records]\\n    if len(set(codes)) != len(codes):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"stream_code repeats; one row per catchment is required\\\")\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":38,\"end_line\":42,\"quoted_text\":\"changes = []\\n    for row in records:\\n        june = float(row[\\\"doc_june_mg_per_l\\\"])\\n        sept = float(row[\\\"doc_sept_mg_per_l\\\"])\\n        changes.append((row[\\\"stream_code\\\"], sept - june))\"}]},{\"description\":\"The row-independent procedure (exact binomial sign test) is applied to the per-stream signs of change, with the number of trials derived from the list of per-stream changes, so the test's n equals the number of independent catchments (24), not the number of water samples (48).\",\"observed_value\":{\"n_units\":24,\"risers\":18,\"fallers\":6,\"ties\":0},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":44,\"end_line\":48,\"quoted_text\":\"n_units = len(changes)\\n    risers = sum(1 for _, delta in changes if delta > 0.0)\\n    fallers = sum(1 for _, delta in changes if delta < 0.0)\\n    ties = n_units - risers - fallers\\n    informative = risers + fallers\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":52,\"end_line\":53,\"quoted_text\":\"outcome = binomtest(risers, informative, 0.5, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\\n    p_value = outcome.pvalue\"}]},{\"description\":\"Independent recomputation from data/input.csv confirms the reported statistics: 18 of 24 streams show a positive September-minus-June change, 6 show a negative change, 0 ties, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value for 18/24 at null probability 0.5 is 2 * 190051/16777216 = 0.02266, matching the reported p = 0.0227 and n = 24.\",\"observed_value\":{\"recomputed_risers\":18,\"recomputed_fallers\":6,\"recomputed_two_sided_p\":0.022656,\"reported_p\":0.0227},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":42,\"end_line\":47,\"quoted_text\":\"- independent catchments analysed: 24\\n- streams with higher September DOC: 18\\n- streams with lower September DOC: 6\\n- ties excluded: 0\\n- proportion of streams increasing: 0.750\\n- exact two-sided p-value: 0.0227\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":49,\"end_line\":49,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided sign test (binomial test, null probability 0.5) on 24 independent proglacial catchments, one paired June-to-September change each: 18 of 24 streams had higher September dissolved organic carbon, proportion 0.750, p = 0.0227, so the 50/50 null is rejected at the 0.05 level.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The dataset does contain repeated measurements of each independent unit (a June and a September DOC value per stream), which is the raw material for the issue class if a workflow were to enter both visits as separate trials; however, this workflow differences the pair into one signed change per stream before testing, so the repeated measurements never enter the sign test as separate observations.\",\"observed_value\":\"two DOC measurements per stream present in wide format; collapsed to one delta before testing\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"The two visits to a stream are repeated measurements of the same unit, so the analysis first subtracts them into one signed change per stream and then tests those twenty-four changes. The paired values are never entered into the test as separate observations, and the number of trials in the test equals the number of streams.\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":6,\"quoted_text\":\"Reads data/input.csv and writes results/report.md. Every catchment occupies\\nexactly one line of the source file, and the pair of visits belonging to a\\nstream is reduced to a single signed change before any test is run, so the\\nsample size of the test equals the number of independent catchments.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to show the opposite verdict by searching for any mechanism through which a single stream could contribute more than one trial to the binomial test: (1) checked all 24 stream_code values in data/input.csv for duplicates (none; each code appears once); (2) inspected the workflow for any long-format expansion that would enter the June and September values as separate observations (none exists; the pair is subtracted into one delta per row before the test); (3) checked whether the test's n could reflect 48 water samples rather than 24 streams (it cannot; n_units = len(changes) = 24 and binomtest receives risers out of risers+fallers = 24); (4) recomputed all 24 deltas, the 18/6/0 split, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value (0.022656 ~ 0.0227), which match the report exactly. Every check failed to produce evidence of repeated independent-unit entry, supporting the no-issue verdict.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-h2-reviewer-fable-38","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:4da6848cdd3a5d975d87","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The input file contains exactly 24 data rows with 24 unique stream_code values (PG01 through PG24), so each independent unit occupies exactly one row and no unit is repeated in the file.","observed_value":{"n_rows":24,"n_unique_stream_codes":24,"duplicates":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":1,"quoted_text":"stream_code,catchment_area_km2,glacier_cover_pct,mean_elev_m,doc_june_mg_per_l,doc_sept_mg_per_l"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"PG01,4.82,31.5,2418,2.14,2.63"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"PG24,18.36,13.8,2071,4.24,3.86"}]},{"description":"The data description designates stream_code as the independent-unit column, defines one trial as one row, and states the paired visits are stored side by side in a single record, so the wide layout keeps repeated measurements out of separate rows.","observed_value":"independent unit = stream_code; one trial = one row; both visits in one record","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"One row is: one proglacial stream, carrying its catchment descriptors together with its single June and its single September dissolved organic carbon measurement\nIndependent unit column: stream_code\nOne trial is: one row"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3,"quoted_text":"Both visit values sit side by side in the same record, so a stream never occupies more than one line of the file."}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly guards against duplicated independent units by raising an error if any stream_code repeats, then reduces each stream's two visits to one signed change so exactly one observation per unit enters the test.","observed_value":"duplicate guard present; one delta per stream computed","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":34,"end_line":36,"quoted_text":"codes = [row[\"stream_code\"] for row in records]\n    if len(set(codes)) != len(codes):\n        raise ValueError(\"stream_code repeats; one row per catchment is required\")"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":38,"end_line":42,"quoted_text":"changes = []\n    for row in records:\n        june = float(row[\"doc_june_mg_per_l\"])\n        sept = float(row[\"doc_sept_mg_per_l\"])\n        changes.append((row[\"stream_code\"], sept - june))"}]},{"description":"The row-independent procedure (exact binomial sign test) is applied to the per-stream signs of change, with the number of trials derived from the list of per-stream changes, so the test's n equals the number of independent catchments (24), not the number of water samples (48).","observed_value":{"n_units":24,"risers":18,"fallers":6,"ties":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":44,"end_line":48,"quoted_text":"n_units = len(changes)\n    risers = sum(1 for _, delta in changes if delta > 0.0)\n    fallers = sum(1 for _, delta in changes if delta < 0.0)\n    ties = n_units - risers - fallers\n    informative = risers + fallers"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":52,"end_line":53,"quoted_text":"outcome = binomtest(risers, informative, 0.5, alternative=\"two-sided\")\n    p_value = outcome.pvalue"}]},{"description":"Independent recomputation from data/input.csv confirms the reported statistics: 18 of 24 streams show a positive September-minus-June change, 6 show a negative change, 0 ties, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value for 18/24 at null probability 0.5 is 2 * 190051/16777216 = 0.02266, matching the reported p = 0.0227 and n = 24.","observed_value":{"recomputed_risers":18,"recomputed_fallers":6,"recomputed_two_sided_p":0.022656,"reported_p":0.0227},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":42,"end_line":47,"quoted_text":"- independent catchments analysed: 24\n- streams with higher September DOC: 18\n- streams with lower September DOC: 6\n- ties excluded: 0\n- proportion of streams increasing: 0.750\n- exact two-sided p-value: 0.0227"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":49,"end_line":49,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided sign test (binomial test, null probability 0.5) on 24 independent proglacial catchments, one paired June-to-September change each: 18 of 24 streams had higher September dissolved organic carbon, proportion 0.750, p = 0.0227, so the 50/50 null is rejected at the 0.05 level."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The dataset does contain repeated measurements of each independent unit (a June and a September DOC value per stream), which is the raw material for the issue class if a workflow were to enter both visits as separate trials; however, this workflow differences the pair into one signed change per stream before testing, so the repeated measurements never enter the sign test as separate observations.","observed_value":"two DOC measurements per stream present in wide format; collapsed to one delta before testing","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":18,"end_line":18,"quoted_text":"The two visits to a stream are repeated measurements of the same unit, so the analysis first subtracts them into one signed change per stream and then tests those twenty-four changes. The paired values are never entered into the test as separate observations, and the number of trials in the test equals the number of streams."},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":3,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"Reads data/input.csv and writes results/report.md. Every catchment occupies\nexactly one line of the source file, and the pair of visits belonging to a\nstream is reduced to a single signed change before any test is run, so the\nsample size of the test equals the number of independent catchments."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show the opposite verdict by searching for any mechanism through which a single stream could contribute more than one trial to the binomial test: (1) checked all 24 stream_code values in data/input.csv for duplicates (none; each code appears once); (2) inspected the workflow for any long-format expansion that would enter the June and September values as separate observations (none exists; the pair is subtracted into one delta per row before the test); (3) checked whether the test's n could reflect 48 water samples rather than 24 streams (it cannot; n_units = len(changes) = 24 and binomtest receives risers out of risers+fallers = 24); (4) recomputed all 24 deltas, the 18/6/0 split, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value (0.022656 ~ 0.0227), which match the report exactly. Every check failed to produce evidence of repeated independent-unit entry, supporting the no-issue verdict.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":27335,"ttft_stream_ms":1482,"time_to_request_ms":10,"type":"result","duration_ms":63265,"uuid":"e6f45cbf-2998-4867-906a-24ce22d20289"}
